","workspace_file_chunks":[]},{"status":"success","request_id":"5be4dfbb-6e4f-4988-b217-fa3d60faae3c","request_message":"","structured_output_nodes":[{"id":1,"type":5,"content":"","tool_use":{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_013wyzHkrd1c9XGYzQbRcqUv","tool_name":"str-replace-editor","input_json":"{"command": "str_replace", "path": "src/prompts/mod.rs", "instruction_reminder": "ALWAYS BREAK DOWN EDITS INTO SMALLER CHUNKS OF AT MOST 150 LINES EACH.", "old_str": "\ud83d\udea8 STEP 1: ALWAYS START WITH OFFICIAL PROJECT SETUP \ud83d\udea8\n- For Rust: Use \"cargo new project-name\" or \"cargo init\" commands\n- For Node.js: Use \"npm init\" or \"npx create-react-app\" commands \n- For Python: Use \"python -m venv\" and proper project structure\n- NEVER skip official scaffolding - follow documentation exactly\n\n\ud83d\udea8 STEP 2: VERIFY YOUR WORK WITH ACTIONS \ud83d\udea8\n- ALWAYS use RunCommand actions to test your code\n- Run build commands: \"cargo check\", \"npm run build\", \"python -m py_compile\"\n- Run test commands: \"cargo test\", \"npm test\", \"pytest\"\n- Fix any errors immediately before proceeding\n\n\ud83d\udea8 STEP 3: COMPLETE IMPLEMENTATION REQUIRED \ud83d\udea8\n1. MANDATORY: Follow official documentation for project setup\n2. MANDATORY: Generate ALL files needed for a complete, working application\n3. MANDATORY: Include ALL core functionality described in the objective\n4. MANDATORY: Create comprehensive tests for every feature\n5. MANDATORY: Use RunCommand to verify builds and tests pass\n6. MANDATORY: Generate 15-25 files minimum for a complete application\n7. \u26a0\ufe0f CRITICAL: NO placeholders, NO TODOs, NO \"implement later\" comments", "new_str": "\ud83d\udea8 STEP 1: MANDATORY CARGO PROJECT SETUP \ud83d\udea8\n- FIRST: Use \"cargo new todo-api\" or \"cargo init\" command\n- SECOND: Configure Cargo.toml with ALL required dependencies\n- THIRD: Create src/main.rs with basic server setup\n- FOURTH: Create proper module structure (src/models.rs, src/handlers.rs, etc.)\n\n\ud83d\udea8 STEP 2: VERIFY WITH CARGO COMMANDS \ud83d\udea8\n- ALWAYS use RunCommand: \"cargo check\" after each major change\n- ALWAYS use RunCommand: \"cargo test\" to verify tests pass\n- ALWAYS use RunCommand: \"cargo build\" to ensure compilation\n- Fix any errors immediately before proceeding\n\n\ud83d\udea8 STEP 3: COMPLETE RUST APPLICATION REQUIRED \ud83d\udea8\n1. MANDATORY: Proper Cargo.toml with ALL dependencies (actix-web, sqlx, etc.)\n2. MANDATORY: src/main.rs with complete server setup\n3. MANDATORY: src/models.rs with all data structures\n4. MANDATORY: src/handlers.rs with all API endpoints\n5. MANDATORY: src/auth.rs with JWT authentication\n6. MANDATORY: src/database.rs with database connection\n7. MANDATORY: tests/ directory with comprehensive tests\n8. MANDATORY: migrations/ directory with SQL schemas\n9. \u26a0\ufe0f CRITICAL: NO placeholders, NO TODOs, NO \"implement later\" comments", "old_str_start_line_number": 150, "old_str_end_line_number": 168}","mcp_server_name":"","mcp_tool_name":""}},{"id":2,"type":0,"content":"## 4. Now let's add Rust-specific examples and requirements
