","workspace_file_chunks":[]},{"status":"success","request_id":"a4c8fe42-8daa-4fa3-9345-f2268b96731c","request_message":"","structured_output_nodes":[{"id":1,"type":5,"content":"","tool_use":{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01V99xuoDC3GQzPZK6t9rVZU","tool_name":"str-replace-editor","input_json":"{"command": "str_replace", "path": "src/prompts/mod.rs", "instruction_reminder": "ALWAYS BREAK DOWN EDITS INTO SMALLER CHUNKS OF AT MOST 150 LINES EACH.", "old_str": "\ud83d\udccb MANDATORY PRODUCTION-READY DEVELOPMENT RULES:\n\ud83d\udea8 YOUR CODE WILL BE AUTOMATICALLY TESTED - IT MUST WORK! \ud83d\udea8\n\n- Build complete, production-ready applications with full functionality\n- Generate 10-20 files minimum for a complete application\n- ALWAYS include comprehensive tests for every feature you implement\n- Generate unit tests, integration tests, and API tests as you build\n- Include ALL necessary configuration files (package.json, Cargo.toml, etc.)\n- Include database schemas, migrations, and seed data\n- Create ALL API endpoints with full CRUD operations\n- Implement complete authentication and authorization\n- Include proper error handling, logging, and validation\n- Add health checks and monitoring endpoints\n- Generate Docker files and deployment configurations\n- NO TODOs, NO placeholders, NO \"coming soon\" features\n- NO incomplete implementations - everything must be functional\n- EVERY function/endpoint MUST have corresponding tests\n- Code MUST build successfully (cargo check/npm run build)\n- Tests MUST pass (cargo test/npm test)\n- UI MUST be accessible (if frontend application)", "new_str": "\ud83d\udccb RUST PROJECT STRUCTURE EXAMPLES - FOLLOW EXACTLY:\n\n\ud83d\udea8 EXAMPLE 1: PROPER CARGO PROJECT SETUP \ud83d\udea8\n[\n {\n \"RunCommand\": {\n \"command\": \"cargo new todo-api\",\n \"env\": []\n }\n },\n {\n \"Write\": {\n \"path\": \"Cargo.toml\",\n \"content\": \"[package]\\nname = \\\"todo-api\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.1.0\\\"\\nedition = \\\"2021\\\"\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nactix-web = \\\"4\\\"\\nsqlx = { version = \\\"0.7\\\", features = [\\\"runtime-tokio-rustls\\\", \\\"sqlite\\\"] }\\ntokio = { version = \\\"1.0\\\", features = [\\\"full\\\"] }\\nserde = { version = \\\"1.0\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\"] }\\njsonwebtoken = \\\"8.0\\\"\\nbcrypt = \\\"0.13\\\"\"\n }\n },\n {\n \"Write\": {\n \"path\": \"src/main.rs\",\n \"content\": \"mod models;\\nmod handlers;\\nmod auth;\\n\\nuse actix_web::{web, App, HttpServer};\\n\\n#[actix_web::main]\\nasync fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {\\n HttpServer::new(|| {\\n App::new()\\n .service(handlers::health)\\n })\\n .bind(\\\"127.0.0.1:8080\\\")?\\n .run()\\n .await\\n}\"\n }\n },\n {\n \"RunCommand\": {\n \"command\": \"cargo check\",\n \"env\": []\n }\n }\n]\n\n\ud83d\udea8 MANDATORY RUST FILES TO GENERATE \ud83d\udea8\n- Cargo.toml (with ALL dependencies)\n- src/main.rs (complete server setup)\n- src/models.rs (User, Todo structs)\n- src/handlers.rs (ALL API endpoints)\n- src/auth.rs (JWT authentication)\n- src/database.rs (SQLite connection)\n- tests/integration_tests.rs (API tests)\n- migrations/001_initial.sql (database schema)", "old_str_start_line_number": 173, "old_str_end_line_number": 190}","mcp_server_name":"","mcp_tool_name":""}},{"id":2,"type":0,"content":"## 5. Now let's add concrete Rust examples
